 ## Overview
-MLPRender_Fea is a neural rendering module that predicts RGB color from input features, view directions, and their positional encodings using a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) [S3, unofficial]. It builds on [NeRF MLP Architecture](910-nerf-mlp-architecture.md) by decoupling the spatial feature representation from the view-dependent color prediction, allowing the MLP to focus solely on mapping features and viewing angles to radiance [S1][S3, unofficial]. Unlike the parent architecture which maps raw 5D coordinates directly to density and color, MLPRender_Fea takes pre-computed features as input, enabling hybrid approaches where features are stored in grids or learned per-image [S1][S3, unofficial].
+MLPRender_Fea is a neural rendering module that predicts RGB color from input features and viewing directions using a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) [S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem of view-dependent appearance modeling by mapping latent feature representations to final pixel colors, distinguishing itself from position-only fields by explicitly incorporating directional information [S3, unofficial]. Unlike its sibling [Position-Only NeRF Field](1253-position-only-nerf-field.md) which ignores view direction, or [Tiny NeRF](1275-tiny-nerf.md) which simplifies the architecture, MLPRender_Fea retains the full directional encoding to capture complex specularities and shading [S3, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
